# Causality, Seriousness, and Expectedness

**Track:** Pharmacovigilance
**Level:** Beginner-friendly
**Estimated time:** 90–120 minutes

## What you need to make

Assess a set of sample cases using a transparent causality method and regulatory seriousness criteria.

## Passing checklist

- [ ] Apply the Naranjo or WHO-UMC framework to each sample case.
- [ ] Classify seriousness criteria and explain the reporting implication.
- [ ] Assess expectedness against a supplied reference document.
- [ ] Put the work and a short explanation in one public or view-only link.

## What to submit

Submit one public or view-only link. Put supporting files in the same repository, folder, or project page so one link is enough.

## Optional portfolio upgrade

Record uncertainty and additional information needed.

## Supplied material

- [Expectedness reference document](https://edvyro.in/datasets/source-materials/task-source-library.html#pv) — The supplied fictional Velunex product reference and four assessment cases.

## Submission example

Share one GitHub repository, Google Drive folder, Figma file, YouTube video, or portfolio page that a reviewer can open without requesting access.
